(* The App theory (registers the REPL app "Minilang.AoA_Learning") plus a tiny toy
   target theory, on a Minilang_AoA base — cheap to build and enough to smoke-test
   the whole harness end-to-end without the MathBench corpus.

   For the real learning run the REPL boots on the MathBench_Prover heap and loads
   AoA_Learning_App FROM SOURCE at runtime (by its qualified name
   "AoA_Learning_Base.AoA_Learning_App", the same way premise-extraction loads its
   app). The App theory imports Minilang_AoA (in the MathBench_Prover heap) +
   Isa_REPL — Minilang_AoA no longer pulls Isa_REPL, so the App declares it
   directly; every REPL server already carries Isa_REPL at launch, so the
   runtime source-load resolves it. *)
session AoA_Learning_Base = Minilang_AoA +
  sessions
    Isa_REPL
  theories
    AoA_Learning_App
    AoA_Learning_Toy
